diff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bc52872
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Design: pre-generated message ids and persisted flag on the chat stream
+
+## Goal
+Clients learn the ids of the turn's messages at the start of the stream, and the final `done`
+event tells them whether the turn was saved, so no separate `error` event is needed.
+
+## Scope
+Included:
+- `ChatService.open_turn` generates a user and an assistant message id (distinct, via `new_id`).
+- `build_turn_messages` takes those ids instead of generating them.
+- First `conversation` event carries `message_id` (assistant id).
+- `done` event carries `message_id` (assistant id, `None` if save failed), `persisted`, `created_at`.
+- `ChatTurnResult` gains `user_message_id`, `assistant_message_id`, `created_at`.
+- Remove `EventType.ERROR`, `ProgressEvent.error`, `ErrorCode.PERSIST_FAILED`, `PERSIST_FAILED_MESSAGE`.
+- CLI `_render` prints `!! Không lưu được lượt hội thoại này.` to stderr on `done` with `persisted` false.
+- README sentence about `PERSIST_FAILED` updated.
+
+Unchanged: persistence semantics (atomic `append_turn`, failure is swallowed and logged),
+`ChatTurnResult.message_id` (still `None` on failed save), DB schema, runner events, other event types.
+
+## Interfaces
+- `ChatSession.__init__(execution, conversation, *, created, user_message_id, assistant_message_id, conversations, clock)`
+- `ChatSession.user_message_id -> str`, `ChatSession.assistant_message_id -> str` (read-only properties)
+- `build_turn_messages(*, conversation_id, run, answer_text, citations, phases, now, user_message_id: str, assistant_message_id: str) -> tuple[Message, Message]`
+- `ChatTurnResult`: adds `user_message_id: str`, `assistant_message_id: str`, `created_at: datetime` (= stored assistant message `created_at`).
+- SSE `conversation`: `{conversation_id, title, created, message_id}`.
+- SSE `done`: runner data plus `{conversation_id, message_id, persisted, created_at (ISO)}`.
+- CLI `_render(event, evidence)`: new branch for `EventType.DONE`.
+
+## Approach
+Ids are generated in `ChatService.open_turn` when the `ChatSession` is created (domain stays pure; ids
+passed down). `ChatSession._persist` passes them to `build_turn_messages`; the result copies them and
+the assistant message's `created_at`. `events()` yields one `done` and nothing after it. The CLI
+drives the runner directly, whose `done` has no `persisted` key; only an explicit `False` triggers the
+warning (via `data.get("persisted") is False`), so absent/true print nothing.
+
+## Testing
+- Domain: `build_turn_messages` uses given ids.
+- Service: distinct ids exposed; conversation event and done event carry them; `created_at` equals stored
+  message's; failed save yields `done` as last event with `persisted` false, `message_id` None, no error.
+- CLI: `_render` stderr output for persisted false / true.
+- Full `uv run pytest`.
